                <pb facs="0526" n="1486" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1486"/>

                <head>No. 1012.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Magee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 13,
                        1888</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 100.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your telegram of the 9th
                    instant, informing me that in compliance with my No. 96, of the 17th ultimo,
                    “Albert Erbers, <hi rendition="#italic">alias</hi> Eberson, is arrested.”</p>
                <p>The governor of Wisconsin and the district attorney of Milwaukee have been so
                    advised.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
